ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
\textbf{Solution:} Let's substitute points A $(-3,0)$ and C $(1,0)$ into $y=ax^{2}+bx-3$, to get
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
0=9a-3b-3 \\
0=a+b-3
\end{array}
\right.
\]
Solving this system, we find
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
a=1 \\
b=2
\end{array}
\right.
\]
$\therefore$ The equation of the parabola is $\boxed{y=x^{2}+2x-3}$.

